    {
      "skill_id": "pt-b2-037",
      "title": "Diminutives, augmentatives and the superlative -íssimo",
      "explanation": "Evaluative suffixes change size or tone. The diminutive -inho or -zinho shows small size or affection: casa gives casinha, livro gives livrinho, pão gives pãozinho, café gives cafezinho, flor gives florzinha, amor gives amorzinho. Use -zinho after a stressed vowel, a nasal sound or a consonant (pão, café, flor, amor), and -inho after an unstressed final vowel, which drops (casa, livro). The augmentative -ão marks large size or intensity: grande gives grandão. The superlative -íssimo means very: bonito gives bonitíssimo, lindo gives lindíssimo, feliz gives felicíssimo, with the c from the stem. Do not form the superlative from the written form of the adjective (felizíssimo is wrong).",
      "examples": [
        {
          "pt": "Ela comprou uma casinha.",
          "en": "She bought a little house."
        },
        {
          "pt": "Você quer um cafezinho?",
          "en": "Would you like a little coffee?"
        },
        {
          "pt": "Ele está felicíssimo.",
          "en": "He is very happy."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["COE-CV20"],
