    {
      "skill_id": "pt-b2-039",
      "title": "Adjective position and ser or estar with adjectives",
      "explanation": "Most adjectives follow the noun, but some change meaning with position. Before the noun they often carry a figurative or personal sense; after it, a literal one. Um grande homem is a great man and um homem grande is a big man; um pobre homem is an unfortunate man and um homem pobre is a man without money; um velho amigo is a friend of long standing and um amigo velho is an elderly friend; um carro novo is a brand-new car and um novo carro is another car. With ser, an adjective states a lasting quality, and with estar a state or a change: ele é chato means he is a boring person, ele está chato means he is being annoying now. Do not use ser for a temporary state (ela é cansada hoje is wrong).",
