      "title": "Spelling reform of 1990",
      "explanation": "The Orthographic Agreement of 1990, in force in Brazil, changed several spellings. The circumflex was dropped in the words ending in -oo and in the forms êem: voo, enjoo, veem, creem, leem. The acute was dropped in the diphthong éi and ói of paroxytone words: ideia, heroico, jiboia. The trema was dropped except in foreign names: frequência, linguiça. Hyphens follow the prefix: no hyphen before a different vowel, or before r or s, which are doubled (autoescola, antirreligioso), and a hyphen before the same vowel or h (micro-ondas, anti-inflamatório). The letters k, w and y are now part of the alphabet. Do not write the old forms (idéia, vôo, vêem), and do not hyphenate where the rule joins the word.",
